<article lang="&language;" id="chomikuj">
<title>chomikuj</title>

<articleinfo>
<authorgroup>
  <author><personname><firstname>kio-chomikuj</firstname><surname>contributors</surname></personname></author>
<!-- TRANS:ROLES_OF_TRANSLATORS -->
</authorgroup>
</articleinfo>

<para>
The <emphasis>chomikuj</emphasis> worker gives KIO applications access to
files stored on <ulink url="https://chomikuj.pl">Chomikuj.pl</ulink> through
its Mobile API v3.
</para>

<para>
Use a URL such as <userinput>chomikuj://<replaceable>account</replaceable>/</userinput>
to browse your own files.  The account is the Chomikuj.pl login name.  The
worker asks for the password through the standard KIO password dialog and can
remember it in KWallet.
</para>

<para>
The URL <userinput>chomikuj:/</userinput> uses the last account configured in
the Chomikuj.pl control module or the last account that was opened
successfully.
</para>

<para>
Public accounts can be browsed read-only with
<userinput>chomikuj://<replaceable>other-account</replaceable>/</userinput>.
The worker signs in with your own account and resolves the other account
through Chomikuj's account search.  Password-protected folders ask for their
folder password.
</para>

<para>
Supported operations are listing, stat, download, upload, folder creation,
rename/move and delete.  There is no timestamp information in the API, listing
sizes are rounded down to whole kilobytes, uploads are implemented as a
delete-after-successful-upload replacement, and copying is implemented as
download plus upload.
</para>

<para>
The read-only <userinput>chomikujstream://<replaceable>account</replaceable>/</userinput>
protocol supports random access through KIO's <function>open</function>,
<function>read</function> and <function>seek</function> operations.  Together
with <ulink url="https://invent.kde.org/system/kio-fuse">kio-fuse</ulink>, it
lets media players stream and seek without downloading the whole file first.
Use the Chomikuj service-menu action or the <command>kio-chomikuj-play</command>
launcher to open a video from the normal <userinput>chomikuj://</userinput>
view.  The streaming protocol is read-only; uploads, renames and deletes stay
on the normal protocol.
</para>

</article>
